Description: Build demographic models, simulate genetic data under the
    coalescent, and infer demographic parameters with approximate Bayesian
    computation (ABC) or neural-network-based supervised machine learning
    (SML). Models are constructed through a Shiny graphical interface and
    simulated with a native C/C++ engine that combines the msABC simulator
    for RADseq-scale data and the vendored scrm SMC-prime simulator for
    whole-genome-scale data. Summary statistics and the joint site
    frequency spectrum are computed in C without intermediate R matrices,
    yielding reference tables compatible with the included ABC rejection
    sampler and with torch-backed neural-network regression and
    classification (model selection). A two-tier out-of-distribution
    diagnostic system flags both prior-predictive coverage failures and
    post-training extrapolation, with integrated-gradient feature
    attribution for classifier-rejected observations. A pre-inference
    diagnostic identifies non-modelled signals (background selection,
    recombination-rate heterogeneity) in empirical whole-genome data.
